  "reason": "Evidence: The current best config (config_019, acc=0.639) uses PCA as the RNA encoder within a multimodal, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted-fusion setup. RNA is clearly the dominant modality (0.591 RNA-only vs 0.208 image-only), and PCA is a simple linear baseline. Uncertainty: It is unknown whether a learned RNA encoder (scvi_n200) can capture non-linear structure that PCA misses, potentially improving the multimodal representation. This experiment (config_031) isolates the RNA encoder as the sole variable—keeping multiprofile, avgpool, ResNet50, and weighted fusion at their validated best settings—directly testing whether scvi_n200 outperforms PCA in the multimodal context. This is the best use of the next budget slot because it addresses the most impactful untested design axis (RNA representation quality) within the already-validated architecture, and the result will determine whether to invest further in learned encoders (scgpt) or pivot to other variables (e.g., image encoder upgrade to ViT-L)."
